ode6.irmos2:
Cleanse me, O Savior,
for many are mine iniquities;
lead me up from the abyss of evils I pray Thee,
for unto Thee have I cried,
and Thou hast hearkened unto me,
O God of my salvation.

ode7.irmos2:
Once in Babylon the fire stood in awe
of God's condescension;
for which sake the youths in the furnace,
dancing with joyous steps as in a meadow, chanted:
O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!
